From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jail: let aarch64 device processes read their thread name

The SIGBUS reporter reads the faulting thread's name with
prctl(PR_GET_NAME) before it prints the address and the mappings. Every
aarch64 device policy allowed only PR_SET_NAME, so a device process that
hit a SIGBUS was killed by seccomp inside the reporter: the log said
"Bad system call" instead of where the fault was. A Windows guest's block
device showed exactly that.

Allow PR_GET_NAME next to PR_SET_NAME in every aarch64 policy that
allows prctl. It only reads the calling thread's own name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/jail/seccomp/aarch64/9p_device.policy b/jail/seccomp/aarch64/9p_device.policy
index c732f3d..9c241cb 100644
--- a/jail/seccomp/aarch64/9p_device.policy
+++ b/jail/seccomp/aarch64/9p_device.policy
@@ -26,4 +26,4 @@ fchown: 1
 fchownat: 1
 fstatfs: 1
 newfstatat: 1
-prctl: arg0 == PR_SET_NAME
+prctl: arg0 == PR_SET_NAME || arg0 == PR_GET_NAME
